---
<p>Go and Bayan share a taste: small languages, plain code, fast builds, one way to format. The differences are in what the compiler checks. Bayan has no <code>nil</code>, no <code>if err != nil</code>, no pointers, and no interface that a type satisfies by accident. This guide maps Go habits to Bayan, then explains what will surprise you.</p>
<p>Every Bayan program on this page was run with the compiler, and the output shown is its real output.</p>

